ARM64EC: Disable native memory callbacks while invalidating guest code.

Full SMC validation can invalidate code directly from the JIT. Erasing
cached translations frees FEX metadata through ntdll, whose memory-free
notifications otherwise reenter the tracker while its code lock is held.
Use the existing scoped callback guard around this internal operation.

Independent M4 repro: rewrite executable code through a writable alias,
with full validation and the empty-code CRC fix. Without this guard the
second call hangs in NtWaitForAlertByThreadId; with it, 1,000 rewrites
complete with zero stale calls. No FH6 gameplay claim.

diff --git a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
index 2312437..90200d6 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
@@ -821,6 +821,9 @@ public:
   }
 
   void InvalidateGuestCodeRange(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread, uint64_t Start, uint64_t Length) override {
+    // Removing cached translations can free FEX's own metadata. Do not reenter
+    // the invalidation tracker through ntdll while its code-cache lock is held.
+    ScopedCallbackDisable Guard;
     InvalidationTracker->InvalidateAlignedInterval(Start, Length, false);
   }
 
